{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.53.6.a001", "note": "מִי יִתֵּן is the multi-source optative idiom rendered by its fixed formula Oh that (rules 17, 30); no morpheme uniquely heads it, so the first token is the display anchor (rule 6).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.001", "WLC.PSA.53.6.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.001", "status": "noncompositional", "target": ["t001", "t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a002", "note": "The ASV's paraphrase supplies a lexical verb of coming for a clause whose Hebrew writes only 'who will give from Zion'; no morpheme licenses it (rule 20). Reading were come as part of יִתֵּן's recasting is the competing reading.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a003", "note": "Supplied the on the construct (rule 29).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a004", "note": "Rule 19.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a005", "note": "מִן → out of heads on out (rule 24).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a007", "note": "Temporal בְּ before infinitive construct takes When (rule 52).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a009", "note": "שׁוּב rendered bringeth back; back completes the lexeme (rule 44). Margin 'returneth to' read and set aside (rule 38).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014", "t015"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a010", "note": "Supplied the on the construct (rule 29).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016", "t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a011", "note": "Rectum takes of, discontinuous around the possessive (rules 19, 25).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018", "t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.012"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a013", "note": "Apodosis Then with no waw in the clause (rule 14).", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a014", "note": "Aligned by clause position: the ASV renders יָגֵל יַעֲקֹב as Jacob rejoice and יִשְׂמַח יִשְׂרָאֵל as Israel be glad, swapping the two verbs' usual glosses.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.013"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022", "t024"], "target_head": "t024"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.014"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a016", "note": "Italic and; the Hebrew clauses are asyndetic (rule 14).", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t025"], "target_head": "t025"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a017", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.53.6.016"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.53.6.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t026"], "target_head": "t026"}, {"id": "PSA.53.6.a018", "note": "Jussive rendered shall be glad; head on the complement